{"sourceSha256": "e30eba06c7b477c7b99209d8be85ac9c23fee5dc1daec671c9833e17b3c66641", "text": "Dear Dr Martinson,\n\nRe: Mr Kenneth Phillips, DOB 05/05/1974\n\n| am writing to refer Mr Philips, a 45-year-old self-employed builder, who is recovering from\n\nbilateral lung transplant surgery and is scheduled to discharge on 01/03/2020. He will be\n\nmoving to Mt Tamborine to live with his sister, who is one of your patients.\n\nMr Phillips is a long-term sufferer of interstitial lung disease, and was admitted to Spint\nHospital on 10/01/2020 to undergo a lung transplant. He has made good progress\npostoperatively and was transferred to the Rehabilitation Ward on 15/02/2020. Initially, he\nWas Quite anxious and reluctant to reduce his oxygen use supply cespite a normal range of\nsaturation after surgery (94-98%). However, after education he has agreed to go home\n\nwithout oxygen.\n\nFollowing the operation, Mr Phillips was commenced on immunosuppressants, which need to\nbe continued. The complete list of his medications is attached to this letter. Mr Phillips has\nacquired a pressure ulcer above the coccyx, which has been treated with daily cressings. His\nsister, as you will be aware, ts a nurse, anc has offered to supervise his medication and\n\nchange fs dressing as required.\n\n| would appreciate your attention to his needs. lf you have any queries, do not hesitate to\n\ncontact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDoctor\n\nWord Count: 199 words", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Dear Dr Martinson,\n\nRe: Mr Kenneth Phillips, DOB 05/05/1974\n\n| am writing to refer Mr Philips, a 45-year-old self-employed builder, who is recovering from\n\nbilateral lung transplant surgery and is scheduled to discharge on 01/03/2020. He will be\n\nmoving to Mt Tamborine to live with his sister, who is one of your patients.\n\nMr Phillips is a long-term sufferer of interstitial lung disease, and was admitted to Spint\nHospital on 10/01/2020 to undergo a lung transplant. He has made good progress\npostoperatively and was transferred to the Rehabilitation Ward on 15/02/2020. Initially, he\nWas Quite anxious and reluctant to reduce his oxygen use supply cespite a normal range of\nsaturation after surgery (94-98%). However, after education he has agreed to go home\n\nwithout oxygen.\n\nFollowing the operation, Mr Phillips was commenced on immunosuppressants, which need to\nbe continued. The complete list of his medications is attached to this letter. Mr Phillips has\nacquired a pressure ulcer above the coccyx, which has been treated with daily cressings. His\nsister, as you will be aware, ts a nurse, anc has offered to supervise his medication and\n\nchange fs dressing as required.\n\n| would appreciate your attention to his needs. lf you have any queries, do not hesitate to\n\ncontact me.\n\nYours sincerely,\n\nDoctor\n\nWord Count: 199 words", "extraction": "ocr", "layout": {"version": 1, "width": 2400.0, "height": 2800.0, "blocks": [{"text": "Dear Dr Martinson,", "lines": [{"text": "Dear Dr Martinson,", "x": 0.01292, "y": 0.01143, "width": 0.19417, "height": 0.0175, "confidence": 0.956, "words": [{"text": "Dear", "x": 0.01292, "width": 0.04792, "confidence": 0.954}, {"text": "Dr", "x": 0.06792, "width": 0.02375, "confidence": 0.96}, {"text": "Martinson,", "x": 0.09708, "width": 0.11, "confidence": 0.954}], "uncertainWords": []}]}, {"text": "Re: Mr Kenneth Phillips, DOB 05/05/1974", "lines": [{"text": "Re: Mr Kenneth Phillips, DOB 05/05/1974", "x": 0.01292, "y": 0.05393, "width": 0.42917, "height": 0.0175, "confidence": 0.958, "words": [{"text": "Re:", "x": 0.01292, "width": 0.03042, "confidence": 0.961}, {"text": "Mr", "x": 0.05208, "width": 0.02708, "confidence": 0.962}, {"text": "Kenneth", "x": 0.08583, "width": 0.08542, "confidence": 0.96}, {"text": "Phillips,", "x": 0.17958, "width": 0.08, "confidence": 0.955}, {"text": "DOB", "x": 0.27, "width": 0.0425, "confidence": 0.958}, {"text": "05/05/1974", "x": 0.31958, "width": 0.1225, "confidence": 0.951}]